# The agent trace store is local, per-developer and regenerable.
# It holds run inputs/outputs; nothing in it belongs in the repository.
agent/observability/runs/

# QA baseline snapshots taken by .agents/skills/legal-site-qa/scripts/baseline.mjs.
# A session artifact recording what the checks said at a point in time, not a
# second home for the recorded baseline in docs/CURRENT-ARCHITECTURE.md §12.
.agents/.qa-baseline.json

# Contract records written by agents. Run artifacts, not canonical data:
# the legal record lives in data/, and nothing reaches it without a human.
agent/records/

# Editorial drafts. Run artifacts in the shape every other agent here
# produces, written where SESSION 14 said to write them; the site is not
# changed because an agent was confident.
agent/proposals/editorial/drafts/

# The health monitor's historical record. Run artifacts, and — the reason this
# entry is not merely conventional — it holds PRIVATE CONTROL PLANE HEALTH DATA:
# which routes answer unauthenticated requests, which approvals were void, which
# gate refused what. This repository has no publication boundary (GitHub Pages
# serves main at the repository root with no _config.yml and no exclude list), so
# a git-tracked health record would be a health record on the public web.
#
# A .gitignore entry is not a security boundary, and agent/health/ says so rather
# than pretending otherwise. It is the strongest control available in a repository
# whose deployment unit is the whole tree.
#
# The public-safe subset is a separate artifact: node agent/health/cli.mjs --publish
#
# Everything in the directory, with the README negated back in — the reasoning for
# the rule belongs in the repository even though nothing it describes does. The
# glob is `*` rather than `*.jsonl` so a future artifact is ignored by DEFAULT:
# an ignore list that only covers the extension somebody thought of is the same
# shape of mistake as a denylist.
agent/health/history/*
!agent/health/history/README.md

# The Control Room's private state: the operator registry and its password
# hashes, live sessions, the approval audit trail, review notes and in-flight
# OIDC logins. None of it belongs in a repository, and this one publishes its
# whole tree.
#
# .control-room/ is ALREADY outside the published surface — a GitHub Pages
# deployment with no _config.yml does not serve a path whose segments begin with
# "." — so this entry is not what keeps the state private on the web. It is what
# keeps it out of git, which is a different and equally necessary thing: an
# operator registry committed by accident is an operator registry in every clone,
# in every fork and in the history forever.
#
# The glob is `*` with the README negated back in, for the same reason
# agent/health/history/ uses that shape: an ignore list that covers only the
# files somebody thought of is the same mistake as a denylist.
.control-room/state/*
!.control-room/state/README.md

# The Orchestrator's workflow journals. One append-only file per workflow,
# holding the ROUTING: which specialist refused what, which gate blocked which
# proposal, which approval was found void. Run artifacts, and control-plane
# ones — this repository publishes its whole tree, so a tracked journal would
# be an operational trace on the public web.
#
# The state is REPLAYED from these files rather than stored, so losing them
# loses history and no authority: a grant lives in
# agent/implement/decisions/decisions.jsonl, which is tracked, and nothing
# here is a second home for it.
#
# The glob is `*` with the README negated back in, the same shape
# agent/health/history/ and .control-room/state/ use, and for the same reason:
# an ignore list covering only the files somebody thought of is a denylist.
agent/orchestrator/state/*
!agent/orchestrator/state/README.md

# SESSION 24's simulation traces, when a run is asked to keep one
# (`node agent/simulation/cli.mjs run --trace <dir>`). By default the run
# writes into a mkdtemp directory and deletes it, so this entry covers only the
# case where somebody deliberately keeps the trace inside the tree.
#
# Every record in such a trace is marked simulated and asserts nothing about EU
# law — but it is still a run artifact, and this repository publishes its whole
# tree. The glob is `*` with the README negated back in, the same shape
# agent/health/history/, .control-room/state/ and agent/orchestrator/state/ use.
agent/simulation/runs/*
!agent/simulation/runs/README.md
